# OpenSpec

Non-trivial changes must use `openspec/changes/<name>/` (proposal, design, tasks).

## Before creating a new change

**Always scan active `openspec/changes/*/` first** (skip `archive/`). Prefer
**merge into an existing change** over a new folder when ANY of these hold:

| Signal | Prefer merge into |
|--------|-------------------|
| Same subdomain / vertical (resume, chat shell, OpenClaw, notes, …) | That change |
| Follow-up / “later change” called out by an open proposal | The parent change |
| Same user-facing surface (ChatPage shell, Settings, Library drawer, …) | The surface change |
| Tiny additive API that only exists to finish an open scope | The open scope |

Only create a **new** folder when the work has a distinct why, different Out
boundary, or would make the parent tasks.md hard to scan (>~1 screen of
unrelated sections). If merging: fold proposal/design/tasks into the target;
delete the old folder; fix doc cross-links (`SYSTEM`, README, digests).

## Lifecycle

- Sync or archive when the change is ready to keep — typically **before commit or PR**
- Also keep `docs/SYSTEM.md` current (and README if user-facing) — see `docs-sync`
- Do not burn a turn syncing half-baked work after every agent stop
- Skip only for trivial typos/comments/tiny docs

A `beforeShellExecution` hook may **ask** on `git commit` / `gh pr create` if
code changed without OpenSpec / SYSTEM (or user-facing code without README).
Sync, then retry.

See `openspec/config.yaml`, `docs/SYSTEM.md`, and `AGENTS.md`.
